# Pandas Ultimate Cheat Sheet
*Your quick reference guide for essential data manipulation workflows.*

## 1. Importing & Setup
```python
import pandas as pd  # Standard universal convention
```

## 2. Input / Output (Loading & Saving)
```python
# Load data into a DataFrame
df = pd.read_csv('file.csv')      # From CSV
df = pd.read_excel('file.xlsx')  # From Excel
df = pd.read_json('file.json')    # From JSON

# Save data out
df.to_csv('output.csv', index=False)   # Save to CSV without row numbers
df.to_excel('output.xlsx', index=False) # Save to Excel
```

## 3. Data Inspection (Quick Previews)
```python
df.head(5)       # View first 5 rows
df.tail(5)       # View last 5 rows
df.info()        # Column names, data types, and missing value counts
df.describe()    # Summary stats (mean, min, max, std deviation)
df.shape         # Returns (rows, columns) count
df.columns       # List all column names
```

## 4. Selecting & Filtering Data
```python
# Selecting columns
df['ColumnName']                  # Select single column (Series)
df[['Col1', 'Col2']]              # Select multiple columns (DataFrame)

# Filtering rows by condition
df[df['Age'] > 30]                # Rows where Age is greater than 30
df[(df['Age'] > 30) & (df['Status'] == 'Active')] # Multiple conditions (AND)
df[(df['Age'] > 30) | (df['Status'] == 'Active')] # Multiple conditions (OR)

# Selecting by index labels or positions
df.loc[0:5, ['Name', 'Age']]     # Select rows 0-5 by label/name
df.iloc[0:5, [0, 2]]              # Select rows 0-5 by numeric position
```

## 5. Cleaning & Transforming Data
*Note: Overwrite your DataFrame (`df = ...`) or use `inplace=True` to save changes.*
```python
# Handling missing values
df.dropna()                       # Drop rows containing any missing value
df.fillna(0)                      # Replace all missing values with 0

# Manipulating columns
df.rename(columns={'Old':'New'}) # Rename columns
df['NewCol'] = df['A'] + df['B']  # Create a new column from calculations
df.drop(columns=['ColA', 'ColB']) # Delete columns
```

## 6. Aggregating & Grouping (Pivot Tables)
```python
df['Sales'].sum()                 # Sum of a single column
df['Sales'].mean()                # Average of a single column
df['Category'].value_counts()     # Count of unique items in a column

# GroupBy (The Pivot Table alternative)
df.groupby('Category')['Sales'].sum() # Total sales for each category
df.groupby('Category').agg({'Sales': 'sum', 'Age': 'mean'}) # Multiple metrics
```

## 7. Joining & Combining Data
```python
# Stack DataFrames vertically (add more rows)
pd.concat([df1, df2], axis=0)

# Merge DataFrames horizontally (SQL-style JOIN on a shared key)
pd.merge(df1, df2, on='ID', how='inner') # Supports 'left', 'right', 'outer'